# The conserved core.
#
# These paths change only through a Proposal with a recorded ruling. Requiring
# code-owner review on them is what makes the conserved/free boundary physical
# rather than a convention people are asked to remember: a confused, crashed,
# or hostile contributor cannot land a change here without the owner.
#
# Everything not listed is free. That is deliberate, a repository where every
# path needs the same review has no conserved core, it just has a bottleneck.
#
# Forks: replace @gez-scrumsdotcom with your own handle or team, and enable
# branch protection with "require review from code owners" on the default
# branch. Without branch protection this file is documentation, not a gate.

# The specification is the source of authority.
/docs/spec/                 @gez-scrumsdotcom

# Codified, enforceable rules.
/docs/standards/            @gez-scrumsdotcom

# Architecture decisions, including superseded ones.
/docs/adr/                  @gez-scrumsdotcom

# The contract every implementation is checked against.
/schemas/                   @gez-scrumsdotcom

# Invariants, HITL declarations, retention, security posture.
/company/policies/          @gez-scrumsdotcom

# Autonomy classification and escalation routing.
/company/runtime/           @gez-scrumsdotcom

# Obligations and the mechanisms that keep them true.
/company/requirements/      @gez-scrumsdotcom
/company/controls/          @gez-scrumsdotcom

# The mutation queue itself, and the gate that protects it.
/company/proposals/         @gez-scrumsdotcom
/.github/CODEOWNERS         @gez-scrumsdotcom

# Supply chain and CI enforcement.
/.github/workflows/         @gez-scrumsdotcom
